# ============================================================================
# COMMENTED RATIONALE
# ============================================================================

# DEVELOPMENT DOCS EXCLUDED BECAUSE:
# - They accumulate large git history
# - They're internal working notes (not user-facing)
# - They change frequently during development
# - They're not needed in production deployments
# - They can confuse git bisect/blame with noise
# - They're better tracked in workspace locally

# PRODUCTION CODE INCLUDED BECAUSE:
# - Mist*.js files are the actual implementation
# - Strategic docs communicate vision to team
# - User manuals are needed for adoption
# - API references are needed for integration
# - Schema is needed for database setup
# - Client/Server code is the actual product

# ============================================================================
# USAGE NOTES
# ============================================================================
#
# To add a file that's normally ignored:
#   $ git add -f <filename>
#
# To see what would be committed:
#   $ git status
#
# To verify before pushing:
#   $ git diff --cached
#   $ git status
#
